caption: INITIATING INCIDENT
campaign-component: initiating-incident

LOCKED: James uses High Magic in the basement of Furui Tokyo’s Imperial Hotel analogue, based loosely on the Frank Lloyd Wright Imperial Hotel.

LOCKED: The spell creates a sphere approximately 100 yards in radius that deals 25d6 damage per second to everything within it.

LOCKED: The spell is persistent for months but is comparatively easy to dispel under normal circumstances.

LOCKED: A fusion reactor is located in the basement complex.

LOCKED: James did not intend the extended earthquake, metropolitan destruction, SPAA increase, or Gate catastrophe.

LOCKED: The direct spell footprint is approximately 0.026 square kilometres. Average damage is 87.5 points per second before considering any later SPAA escalation. Unprotected ordinary people in the direct zone are almost universally killed during the opening seconds.

LOCKED: The direct zone is destroyed long before the Queen of Cai or another major magical authority could arrive to dispel the original effect.

LOCKED: The spell causes a real earthquake through supernatural resonance and Rift feedback rather than through an ordinary physical conversion of spell damage into seismic energy.

LOCKED: The fusion reactor does not produce a fission-style nuclear detonation. Its failure creates a violent local industrial accident involving stored energy, fire, structural damage, tritium release, and contaminated debris.
